  "slug": "learning-biology-small-c2ee",
  "summary": "Protocol-matched benchmarks now test whether molecular encoders and labels hold up under leakage-aware, chemistry-aware splits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlled, protocol-matched evaluation of machine learning for molecular properties. PeptSol supplies 1388 curated protected-peptide solubility measurements with chemistry-aware splits and benchmarks seven frozen molecular encoders against them. Ark-ADMET shows that representation and hyperparameter choice are endpoint-specific, matching or beating leaderboard scores on 7 of 21 endpoints under the TDC protocol. The immunogenicity study questions the label basis itself: a format lookup beats sequence predictors for ADA% labels across an extended 231-therapeutic dataset. The DiffDock post-training study finds that focused torsional supervision did not provide the expected advantage over broad score-field continuation, reinforcing that geometric relevance alone is insufficient. EpiRank and the pocket-coengagement drug-interaction study extend the same discipline to interface and interaction prediction, using leakage controls and background comparisons. What is new is the emphasis on evaluation design and label quality rather than on architecture.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-06"
}
